`ls` takes four of eza's ideas, written anew for Dukovo (ADR 0440), none
of which changes what GNU's ls prints unless it is asked for:

- `--header`: a line of column titles over the long listing.
- `--octal`: each mode as four octal digits, `0755`, before its letters.
- `--field-colors[=WHEN]`: the long listing's permission letters, sizes
  and times coloured by what they say (read, write and run; small, big
  and huge; today and old), from `LS_FIELD_COLORS`. By default only when
  the names are coloured and only on a terminal, so `--color=always`
  into a pipe stays as GNU's.
- `--icons[=WHEN]`: a Nerd Font icon before each name, by its type and
  ending; off by default, and on a terminal only for `--icons` alone.

The code is in fields.rs and icons.rs; display.rs calls it where the
long listing writes each column. Dukovo only.

